␀␀How tiles work:
The map is built from 256Г—256 "slippy" tiles. Only the tiles for the area you're viewing are fetched вЂ” there is no bulk pre-download.

Because this device can't do HTTPS (not enough heap after Wi-Fi starts) and decodes JPEG far more cheaply than PNG, tiles come from the wadamesh proxy: it fetches the upstream PNG over HTTPS with an identifying User-Agent, re-encodes it as JPEG, and caches it. Your device then caches each tile to its own flash, so a tile is only downloaded once.

Use Options в†’ Reload tiles to re-download the tiles currently in view if one looks corrupted.␀␀пЃё␀Sort by␀п‹­  Select to delete␀␀␀Sort discovered␀Filter␀␀Repeaters␀␀␀Peers␀␀␀Favorites␀␀␀Has location␀␀␀␀Direct (0-hop)␀␀Commands␀␀␀␀~%lu ms / 40 B␀␀%uMHz В· RAM %u%% В· PSRAM %u%% В· %s␀␀␀%a %d %b %Y␀Build %s␀␀␀␀disc␀␀␀␀disc%d␀␀Kees␀␀␀␀Choose an image␀Editing␀99+␀Launcher␀␀␀␀Home button opens␀␀␀Widgets␀App drawer␀␀App icons␀␀␀Compact␀Large␀␀␀о…‚␀Advert␀␀Send advert␀flood␀␀␀nearby␀␀to nodes in range␀␀␀%s %u%%␀up %s␀␀␀PSRAM␀␀␀%s %d%% В· %s␀␀␀radio2 is off␀␀␀heard just now␀␀none heard lately␀␀␀On␀␀MediaMesh␀␀␀%s В· %.3f MHz %.0f kHz␀photos & voice␀␀listening␀␀␀photo...␀␀␀␀no photo␀␀␀␀Latest photo␀␀␀␀No photo yet␀␀␀␀%s В· %s␀␀␀␀Voice & talk␀␀␀␀No voice message yet␀␀␀␀Talk␀␀␀␀Voice␀␀␀PTT␀0123456789ABCDEF␀␀␀␀muted␀␀␀audio unavailable␀␀␀codec␀␀␀[VOX] voice playback couldn't start: %s
